engraving and 'You may wish for an object. --More--'.

'2 blessed scrolls of charging', please. Got em.
z C 'blessed +3 silver dragon scale mail', please. Got it.
z C, Nothing happens. OK, charge up. So it was WoW (0,2).

z C, 'blessed fixed +3 speed boots', please. Got +0 ones.
z C, 'blessed fixed +3 helm of brilliance', please. Got 'a scroll 
labeled VER YED HORRE'. I checked every time my spelling before pressing 
the enter so OI know that I didn't make a spelling mistake. But there 
might be a reason for the fluke, don't know.

The keyboard handler that I use for my win32 tty-port is Ray Chason's 
keyboard handler. The reason for that is it's the only keyboard handler 
(of those three supplied) that handles my finnish keyboard correctly. 
But it locks up, doesn't recognise all keypresses etc. Have to be 
careful playing but that's ok for nethack anyways.

The other reason might be that while I was wishing that helm and 
checking that I've made no spelling mistakes up comes a popup from 
email-client that I have new mail.

Nevertheless one wish wasted (the scroll was uncursed scroll of 
teleportation).

Try again for the HoB and got it. Last wish was wrested from the wand 
and got me blessed spellbook of identify.

By being able to identify everything makes the logistc nightmare much 
much easier to endure.

Then level four has this enormous (9x6) used armor shop that normally 
would have made me salivating but geared up as I was it wasn't so 
exiting. Lot's of identifying done and got the identify for 0% failure. 
Got a blessed +0 pair of leather gloves from it.

Entrance to the mines was also on level four and so Lyra and her new 
companion little dog named Koira went to the mines. First level was lit 
and just a few paces from the stairs was a bag.

The bag was identified as uncursed bag of holding and I saved the game 
and went to sleep.

I've never ascended as I tend to forget that wizard-mode is for testing. 
Now I try not to do any testing in this game.

